{"content":[{"c":["MERIBBAAL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Original name for Mephibosheth, the handicapped son of Jonathan (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.34","r":"1Chr.8.34","rawR":"1Chr.8.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.34","value":"1Chr.8.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.40","r":"1Chr.9.40","rawR":"1Chr.9.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.40","value":"1Chr.9.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:40"},"). The name means “Baal contends” and is displaced by the later name (Mephibosheth, meaning “idol breaker”) in ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.4.4","r":"2Sam.4.4","rawR":"2Sam.4.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.4.4","value":"2Sam.4.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 4:4"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.9.6","r":"2Sam.9.6","rawR":"2Sam.9.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.9.6","value":"2Sam.9.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:6"},". The substitution of ",{"c":["bosheth"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," (“shame”) for ",{"c":["baal"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," (“lord”) was not uncommon when the term acquired its idolatrous connotation (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.11.21","r":"2Sam.11.21","rawR":"2Sam.11.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.11.21","value":"2Sam.11.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 11:21"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Mephibosheth_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Mephibosheth_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Mephibosheth_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mephibosheth #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Meribbaal","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.34","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.34","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.34"},{"anchorText":"9:40","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.40","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.40","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.40"},{"anchorText":"2 Samuel 4:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.4.4","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.4.4","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.4.4"},{"anchorText":"9:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.9.6","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.9.6","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.9.6"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 11:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.11.21","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.11.21","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.11.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c569a82557f33a8b47508768f473d22f3367953cc698dc5e3a265aaf3c14f294","sourceItemName":"Meribbaal","sourceItemOrder":263,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Meribbaal","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Meribbaal","title":"Meribbaal","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}